      "question": "If 4 x = 7 y = 28 -z , then which option is correct? &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 4 x = 7 y = 28 -z , &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If 4<sup>x</sup> = 7<sup>y</sup> = 28<sup>-z</sup>, then which option is correct?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 4<sup>x</sup> = 7<sup>y</sup> = 28<sup>-z</sup>, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "1/x - 2/y - 2/z = 0 1/x - 2/y - 2/z = 0",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1/x  -  2/y  -  2/z = 0</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/x  -  2/y  -  2/z = 0</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "1/x + 2/y + 1/z = 0 1/x + 2/y + 1/z = 0",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1/x + 2/y + 1/z = 0</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/x + 2/y + 1/z = 0</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "2/x + 1/y - 1/z = 0 2/x + 1/y - 1/z = 0",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">2/x + 1/y  -  1/z = 0</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2/x + 1/y  -  1/z = 0</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0 1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>4<sup>x</sup> = 7<sup>y</sup> = 28<sup>-z</sup></p><p>Let 4<sup>x</sup> = 7<sup>y</sup> = 28<sup>-z</sup> = k</p><p>4 = k<sup>1/x</sup>............(i)</p><p>7 = k<sup>1/y</sup>............(ii)</p><p>28 = k<sup>-1/z</sup>...........(iii)</p><p>4 * 7 = 28</p><p>k<sup>1/x</sup> * k<sup>1/y</sup> = k<sup>-1/z</sup>............using eq(i), (ii) and (iii)</p><p>k<sup>1/x</sup> <sup>+ 1/y</sup> = k<sup>-1/z</sup></p><p>1/x + 1/y = -1/z</p><p>1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0</p>",
